WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:06.539
Sometimes a TV show can make big cast shifts
and not suffer too many consequences, but

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.180
others aren't so lucky.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:13.269
These major TV shows just couldn't recover
from the loss and replacement of a major character,

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:16.289
or the actor who played them.

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:23.349
Dallas had its fair share of character replacements
during its run from 1978 to 1991, as any show

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:26.519
that airs for 14 seasons inevitably does.

00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:31.659
But one that still stands out with fans to
this day is the role of Miss Ellie Ewing.

00:00:31.659 --> 00:00:37.590
Barbara Bel Geddes originated the part and
played it right up until 1984, when she left

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.200
in order to have a quadruple bypass heart
surgery.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.790
At the time she was replaced by Donna Reed,
and fans were not into it.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:49.890
In fact, fans were so not into it that six
months later, when Bel Geddes had recovered,

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.150
she was asked back onto the show.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.250
Reed didn't go down without a fight, though
— she tried to sue and halt production.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.579
In the end, the judge didn't agree with her
and the series carried on.

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:04.940
Bel Geddes continued playing Miss Ewing for
the remainder of the series, bringing life

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.130
to the character for over 300 episodes.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:14.640
When Suits hit airwaves in 2011, critics had
positive but somewhat mixed reviews on the

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.540
premise, which turned the tired legal drama
format on its head with the introduction of

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:25.020
Mike Ross, a wannabe lawyer without a degree,
and Harvey Specter, the hotshot attorney who

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.159
mentored him.

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:30.690
Shot in Toronto, the series wound up being
a massive hit for the network, and was considered

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.670
the last of its blue-skies era.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.810
"Hey, you ready for this?"

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.700
"Yeah, I am."

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.369
However, that all ended in 2017, when Patrick
J. Adams and Meghan Markle, who played Mike

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:48.460
Ross and his love interest Rachel Zane respectively,
announced they were leaving the show after

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.840
seven seasons.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:55.050
At that point another original series star,
Gina Torres, also exited, leaving the cast

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.990
down three members.

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:01.880
As a result, the show brought on Dulé Hill
and Katherine Heigl, while upping Amanda Schull

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.250
from recurring to full-time status in season
8.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:09.780
However, the new mix of characters didn't
resonate as well as the old school ones, and

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.370
the show wrapped for good in season 9.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:17.670
It seems like networks have been trying to
recreate the soapy primetime success of Desperate

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.770
Housewives ever since that show went off the
air in 2012.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:27.620
ABC thought it came close with the 2013 entry
Mistresses, which failed to earn critical

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.410
praise but still snagged a second-season renewal
following its steamy first-season summer run.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:37.140
Fans continued to bake in the hotness of it
all the following summer, but when the show

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:42.360
was renewed for a third season, ABC revealed
it was moving production from Los Angeles

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.360
to Vancouver.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:48.890
That was bad news for star Alyssa Milano,
who couldn't be that far from her family.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.800
Milano stepped away as a result, and the show
recruited Jennifer Esposito to fill that void

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.950
with her Calista Raines character.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:01.580
That lasted one season and then Esposito also
left the series in order to pursue other projects.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:06.250
Surprisingly, the show was renewed for one
more season, but without Milano fans just

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:11.319
didn't seem that into it and the series was
axed for good after a very dramatic season

00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:12.599
4 finale.

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:17.190
It's no secret that Julie Benz did not want
to exit Dexter.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:21.250
After she was killed off in the show's fourth
season, she admitted to reporters that she,

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.630
quote, "bawled" and said it was the worst
thing to ever happen to her in her career.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.890
It seems as though fans felt the same way.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.580
While the decision was purely a creative one,
the salt in the wound for passionate viewers

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:38.660
came in season 5 when Julia Stiles was cast
as Lumen Pierce, a new love interest for Dexter.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:43.390
The character lasted the entire season, and
finally exited ahead of season 6.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:47.860
For many it was a turning point, especially
as they watched the show go on to cast other

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:52.709
guest stars, like Colin Hanks and Yvonne Strahovski,
to fill the void.

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:57.940
Then, writers eventually went so far as to
almost pair Dexter up with his adoptive sister

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:58.940
Deb.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:03.340
Now, with the belated Showtime revival on
the way, fans are hoping that the series finally

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.510
doles out a much more satisfying series finale.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:12.730
Chemistry is particularly important when casting
a family sitcom, so fans were a little concerned

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:18.030
when Julia Butters left American Housewife
as the youngest Otto child ahead of its fifth-season

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.030
premiere.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:23.930
Butters brought a notable charm to the character
of Anna-Kat Otto, so much so that when Quentin

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:29.620
Tarantino saw her on his screen he cast her
as serious young actress Trudi in Once Upon

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.100
A Time in Hollywood.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:35.590
That gig wound up being a game-changer for
the young actor, because all kinds of subsequent

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:39.690
offers came in and she left the ABC series
to pursue them.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:45.190
In turn, American Housewife snatched up Giselle
Eisenberg, fresh from her four-season run

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:47.380
on the CBS sitcom Life in Pieces.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:52.590
While Eisenberg is undeniably talented, it's
been hard for fans to adapt to the change

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:56.210
following the show's return in 2020.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.500
"Yeah...kids change."

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.730
All the witty meta jokes in the world won’t
convince viewers to keep watching.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:08.500
The season 5 finale ended up being a series
finale -- ABC canceled American Housewife

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:09.500
in 2021.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:15.860
It's no secret that the children on Tim Allen's
Last Man Standing changed pretty drastically

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:17.150
over the show's run.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:22.530
Amanda Fuller joined the project in season
two as Kristin Baxter, replacing Alexandra

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.979
Krosney, who originated the role.

00:05:24.979 --> 00:05:29.210
Then there's the fact that four different
actors have played the part of Kristin's son

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:31.780
Boyd as the character has aged over the years.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:36.810
But it was Molly Ephraim's exit from the series
following season six that really threw Last

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.009
Man Standing fans for a loop.

00:05:39.009 --> 00:05:44.449
As middle child Mandy, Ephraim had her share
of meaty storylines that made her a show fixture.

00:05:44.449 --> 00:05:50.640
But when ABC canceled Last Man Standing in
2017 and Fox revived it for a seventh-season

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.530
run, Ephraim didn't go with it.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:55.650
She had signed up for new projects, and was
unable to return.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:06:00.680
Molly McCook was cast in her place, and although
the series lasted three seasons on Fox before

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:04.889
its cancelation in 2021, the character was
just never the same.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:11.560
Now this is a story all about how the casting
on Fresh Prince got turned upside down.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:16.070
Fans everywhere are familiar with the behind-the-scenes
strife that went down between Will Smith and

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:21.199
original Aunt Viv actress Janet Hubert, who
played the role for three notable seasons

00:06:21.199 --> 00:06:25.789
before refusing to renew her contract under
what she considered to be a bad deal.

00:06:25.789 --> 00:06:31.259
As a result she exited the show, and she was
replaced by Daphne Maxwell Reid — an actor

00:06:31.259 --> 00:06:35.169
who was originally considered for the role
but refused to audition because a TV show

00:06:35.169 --> 00:06:38.150
starring a young rapper didn't sound like
her thing.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:41.940
"There are a lot of sick, demented perverts
out there."

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.600
"Greetings, all."

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:48.229
Although The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air went
on for three more seasons with the new Aunt

00:06:48.229 --> 00:06:51.410
Viv, there was no replacing Hubert's comedic
timing.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:56.770
Later, when Smith got the gang back together
for the 2020 reunion, he and Hubert sat down

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.750
for the first time to finally iron things
out.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:04.430
The result was the two Aunt Vivs meeting for
the very first time, as many fans wondered

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:07.880
what the show could have been had Hubert stayed
on after all.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.759
When the sixth season of this comedy kicked
off in 1969, viewers were left twitching harder

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:19.740
than Samantha and her magical nose when Emmy
nominee Dick York was suddenly gone as Darrin

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:20.740
Stephens.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:25.880
In his place was Dick Sargent, and fan speculation
as to what happened kicked into overdrive.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:30.710
As it turned out, York had previously injured
his back pretty badly while shooting a movie,

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:34.490
and the pain led him down a dark path of prescription
pills.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:38.890
Eventually he realized he had to leave the
show, and his career never really recovered.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.050
As for Sargent?

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:44.090
He stayed in the role until the series finale
in 1972.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:48.009
Many fans felt the series wasn't the same,
though, and it's worth noting that although

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:54.319
Sargent won a Most Irreplaceable Replacement
TV Land Award in 2006, he was never nominated

00:07:54.319 --> 00:07:56.470
for an Emmy Award like his predecessor.

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.669
Have you heard the one about the two Beckys?

00:07:59.669 --> 00:08:05.061
When Roseanne kicked off its first iteration
back in 1988, it was actor Lecy Goranson who

00:08:05.061 --> 00:08:09.150
originated the role of Becky, the eldest child
to Dan and Roseanne.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:14.729
Fast forward to season five, though, and Goranson
had enrolled in college, and as a result she

00:08:14.729 --> 00:08:19.300
was only available to film part-time, usually
for a phone conversation.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:23.680
The following year producers wanted Becky
back in a more permanent role, so they recast

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:24.849
her with Sarah Chalke.

00:08:24.849 --> 00:08:30.860
That was fine, but things got complicated
when Goranson briefly returned in Season 8

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.010
after finishing school.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:36.399
The following year Chalke was back in the
role, and "the two Beckys" became a running

00:08:36.399 --> 00:08:38.029
thing that frustrated some viewers.

00:08:38.029 --> 00:08:43.510
To their relief, both actors were asked back
for the Roseanne revival in 2018, but only

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:45.790
Goranson returned to play Becky.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:50.579
Producers hired Chalke to instead play a character
named Andrea, who asked Becky to be her surrogate

00:08:50.579 --> 00:08:53.209
in a clever wink to the whole situation.

00:08:54.209 --> 00:08:59.040
For five and a half seasons, Nashville fans
followed Connie Britton's superstar character,

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.329
Rayna Jaymes, as she balanced motherhood,
singing, and reconnecting with her one true

00:09:03.329 --> 00:09:04.850
love, Deacon Claybourne.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:11.300
But that all came crashing down when Britton
shocked fans and exited the series in 2017

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.220
with a devastating storyline that left her
family all alone.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:19.040
It turned out Britton was ready for a change,
but she was having a hard time letting go

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.601
of the people she worked with.

00:09:20.601 --> 00:09:25.929
So when CMT revived Nashville for a fifth
season after ABC axed it at the end of its

00:09:25.929 --> 00:09:30.379
run in 2016, Britton decided it was finally
time to move on.

00:09:30.379 --> 00:09:34.679
After the fictional singer's death there were
plenty of other characters to root for, and

00:09:34.679 --> 00:09:36.920
the show may have ultimately survived.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:42.129
But then the writers introduced Kaitlin Doubleday
as Jessie Caine, a new love interest for Deacon,

00:09:42.129 --> 00:09:45.069
and loyal fans were definitely not happy.

00:09:45.069 --> 00:09:50.309
The series took a bit of a dive, and season
6 ultimately wound up being the last.

00:09:51.309 --> 00:09:54.689
Throughout its eight-season run, House had
a history of replacing characters to switch

00:09:54.689 --> 00:09:59.779
up the storyline and keep things fresh, but
Season 7 is when the casting situation really

00:09:59.779 --> 00:10:01.149
got out of control.

00:10:01.149 --> 00:10:06.499
That year, Olivia Wilde took a leave of absence
from her fan-favorite gig as Thirteen to film

00:10:06.499 --> 00:10:12.279
Cowboys &amp; Aliens, while original actor Lisa
Edelstein announced her departure as Dr. Lisa

00:10:12.279 --> 00:10:13.279
Cuddy.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:17.120
Considering the shakeups, it seemed pretty
clear to longtime fans that the series was

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.129
nearing its expiration date.

00:10:19.129 --> 00:10:24.439
To try and inject new life into the show,
producers hired Odette Annable and Charlyne

00:10:24.439 --> 00:10:29.600
Yi to play the latest fellows alongside Amber
Tamblyn, but the new crew never quite lived

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:34.250
up to the original cast, and as season 8 was
in progress, Fox announced that it would also

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.820
be the show's last.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:41.689
Today Beverly Hills 90210 is also known as
TV's most famous zip code.

00:10:41.689 --> 00:10:46.420
But before the show earned that status, its
original cast had to win over primetime fans

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:49.459
with its older actors and soapy storylines.

00:10:49.459 --> 00:10:55.000
Enter Jason Priestley and Shannen Doherty
as the famous Walsh twins, Brandon and Brenda.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:59.629
From the start, fans were into their chemistry
with the show's other original cast members,

00:10:59.629 --> 00:11:02.480
but behind the scenes it was a different story.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:06.559
Reports of on-set tension between Doherty
and the rest of the cast — specifically

00:11:06.559 --> 00:11:12.399
Jennie Garth — surfaced, and in 1994, Doherty
was axed from the show for good.

00:11:12.399 --> 00:11:17.410
That year she was replaced by Tiffani Thiessen,
who had her own fanbase from her days as Kelly

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.509
on Saved by the Bell.

00:11:18.509 --> 00:11:23.420
But not all fans were into the new character,
Valerie Malone, a family friend of the Walshes.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:28.220
It was clear Val was meant to replace Brenda,
but Saved by the Bell fans weren't sure how

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.040
to receive this new, adult version of the
actor.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:34.949
Meanwhile, the character had her moments,
but she was no Brenda, and the tone of the

00:11:34.949 --> 00:11:36.860
series changed with her casting.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:42.940
She stayed on for most of the rest of the
series, but to this day you can ask any 90210

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:47.809
fan which character they relate to most, and
you probably won't find many Valerie stans

00:11:47.809 --> 00:11:49.569
out there.

